# Odoo OWL Rule

## Version pin
- Detect version first (`${ODOO_VERSION}` or nearest `__manifest__.py`). Primary: **16–19**.
- Offline cheat-sheet: `skills/odoo-invariants.md`
- OWL: v16–v18 OWL 2.x; v19+ OWL 3.x (stricter static props). (v14–15 limited / different.)

## Stable syntax (v16–v19)
- `/** @odoo-module **/`
- `import { Component, useState } from "@odoo/owl"`
- `import { useService } from "@web/core/utils/hooks"` (not `@odoo/owl`) — confirmed `web/static/src/core/utils/hooks.js` on **v16, v17, v18, v19**
- `import { registry } from "@web/core/registry"` for actions / systray / services
- Register assets under `web.assets_backend` (or website bundles) in `__manifest__.py`
- Do not invent hooks (e.g. fictional `useVisible` / `useIntersectionObserver`)

## Verify with MCP-code when needed
- Prefer `codemode_search` → `codemode_execute` with pinned `version` (`odoo.compact.frontend_brief`, `owl_components`, `owl_templates`).
- Keep components small; sanitize `t-esc`; do not expose secrets in templates.
